+# Third-Party Technical Privacy Audit & Mitigation Report
+
+**Application**: The Daily Grind Artisanal Coffee  
+**Date**: October 2026  
+**Auditor**: Privacy by Design Engineering  
+**Standard**: Web Privacy & Security Guidelines (ISO/IEC 27701 & Modern Web Privacy Standards)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+This audit evaluates all third-party integrations, external assets, and data flows within The Daily Grind application. In accordance with the **Privacy by Design** and **Trustworthy Agency** principles, we enforce zero passive third-party tracking, strict purpose limitation, data minimization, and browser-enforced isolation.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Third-Party Inventory & Risk Assessment
+
+| Service / Resource | Purpose | Risk Profile | Former Behavior | Privacy-Preserving Mitigation | Status |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| **Video Hosting (YouTube)** | Coffee roasting craft showcase | **High** (Third-party tracking cookies, canvas fingerprinting, passive telemetry) | Interactive iframe loaded on initial page load | **Façade Pattern**: Static poster thumbnail displayed. Iframe with `youtube-nocookie.com` only loaded upon explicit user click | **Enforced** |
+| **Social Sharing (X / Facebook / etc.)** | User content sharing | **High** (Third-party SDKs load tracking scripts and beacon user browsing behavior) | Third-party JS SDK (`widgets.js` / `sdk.js`) loaded | **Static HTML Links**: Clean `https://x.com/intent/tweet` anchor links with `rel="noopener" target="_blank"` with zero external scripts | **Enforced** |
+| **Identity Providers (Google / Apple / Auth)** | Account sign-in | **Medium** (IdP tracking relying parties before user consent) | Redirect or third-party button iframe | **FedCM (Federated Credential Management API)**: Native browser-mediated credential negotiation preventing IdP cross-site tracking | **Enforced** |
+| **Imagery (Unsplash)** | Hero and seasonal coffee photography | **Low** (Referrer leakage, IP exposure) | Standard `<img>` with default referrer | Strict `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin` and restrictive CSP `img-src` domain allowlist | **Enforced** |
+| **Embedded State / Cookies** | Embedded widgets | **Medium** (Cross-site user tracking via 3rd-party cookies) | Standard third-party cookies | **CHIPS (Partitioned Cookies)**: `Partitioned; Secure; HttpOnly` to prevent cross-site identity leakage | **Enforced** |
+
+---
+
+## 3. Detailed Mitigation Strategies
+
+### 3.1 Façade Pattern for Media Embeds
+- **Problem**: Loading external video or media embeds immediately transmits user IP addresses, browser fingerprints, and existing cookies to third parties before the user ever engages with the content.
+- **Solution**: The application displays a static thumbnail and play button. Only when the user explicitly clicks the play button does the application inject the iframe pointing to `https://www.youtube-nocookie.com`.
+- **Code implementation**:
+  ```html
+  <div id="video-facade" class="facade-container" data-video-id="abc123">
+    <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1501339847302-ac426a4a7cbb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80" alt="Play Roasting Demonstration">
+    <button class="facade-play-btn" aria-label="Play video">▶ Watch Our Roasting Process</button>
+  </div>
+  ```
+
+### 3.2 Privacy-Preserving Social Sharing
+- **Problem**: Vendor social buttons (e.g., Facebook Like, Twitter Tweet) execute external JavaScript that tracks user navigation across the web.
+- **Solution**: Completely eliminate third-party scripts. Utilize static web intents with `rel="noopener" target="_blank"`.
+- **Code implementation**:
+  ```html
+  <a href="https://x.com/intent/tweet?text=The%20Daily%20Grind%20Coffee&url=https%3A%2F%2Fdailygrind.example.com" 
+     rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="share-link">
+     Share on X
+  </a>
+  ```
+
+### 3.3 Federated Credential Management (FedCM)
+- **Problem**: Traditional third-party identity providers observe user visits across multiple websites even before the user decides to log in.
+- **Solution**: Implement `navigator.credentials.get({ identity: { providers: [...] } })` so that identity mediation is handled natively by the user agent without leaking user browsing behavior to the IdP.
+
+### 3.4 Cookies Having Independent Partitioned State (CHIPS)
+- **Problem**: Unpartitioned cookies can be accessed across distinct top-level contexts, enabling cross-site tracking.
+- **Solution**: Any contextual cookies use the `Partitioned` attribute:
+  `Set-Cookie: theme_pref=light; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Partitioned; HttpOnly`
+
+---
+
+## 4. Continuous Monitoring & Network Auditing Protocol
+
+1. **Automated Header Verification**: Verify on deployment that `Permissions-Policy`, `Content-Security-Policy`, and `Referrer-Policy` strictly govern resource fetching.
+2. **HAR File Auditing**: Inspect all outbound network requests on staging environments using DevTools HAR analysis to guarantee that zero unauthorized third-party beacons or scripts are introduced.
+3. **No LocalStorage for PII**: Maintain zero PII or auth credentials in `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`.
